# Minecraft 26.x uses Mojang mappings, not Yarn

Yarn is no longer published past 1.21.11. This project compiles against **official Mojang
mappings**, so always use mojmap names: `PathfinderMob` (not `MobEntity`), `Level` (not `World`),
`Mob.createMobAttributes()`, `BuiltInRegistries`.

## `ResourceLocation` was renamed to `Identifier`

```java
// ❌ BAD
import net.minecraft.resources.ResourceLocation;
ResourceLocation id = ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath(MOD_ID, "silverleos");

// ✅ GOOD
import net.minecraft.resources.Identifier;
Identifier id = Identifier.fromNamespaceAndPath(MOD_ID, "silverleos");
```

## Entity types are built from a `ResourceKey`

`EntityType.Builder#build` takes the `ResourceKey`, so declare the key first and reuse it.

```java
public static final ResourceKey<EntityType<?>> SILVERLEOS_KEY =
        ResourceKey.create(Registries.ENTITY_TYPE, Silverleos.id("silverleos"));

public static final EntityType<SilverleosEntity> SILVERLEOS = Registry.register(
        BuiltInRegistries.ENTITY_TYPE, SILVERLEOS_KEY,
        EntityType.Builder.of(SilverleosEntity::new, MobCategory.CREATURE)
                .sized(0.9f, 0.7f)
                .build(SILVERLEOS_KEY));
```

Register attributes separately via `FabricDefaultAttributeRegistry.register(TYPE, Entity.createAttributes())`.

## Register renderers with vanilla `EntityRenderers`

Fabric's `EntityRendererRegistry` is deprecated in full; the transitive access widener exposes the
vanilla method instead.

```java
// ❌ BAD — deprecated
EntityRendererRegistry.register(ModEntities.SILVERLEOS, SilverleosRenderer::new);

// ✅ GOOD
EntityRenderers.register(ModEntities.SILVERLEOS, SilverleosRenderer::new);
```

Client-only code belongs in `src/client/java` (the build uses `splitEnvironmentSourceSets()`).
